---
/*
 * The architecture diagram: one inline SVG whose colors all come from the tokens, its legend,
 * and the five numbered steps the diagram's orange markers refer to. The SVG keeps a fixed
 * min-width and scrolls inside .dg-wrap on narrow screens.
 */
import SectionHead from "./SectionHead.astro";
---
<section class="s" id="arch">
  <SectionHead num="§03" kicker="Architecture" title="No hosted service in the middle">
    {/* design.md §1 (Tailscale the only way in; outbound open), §2 System overview (core calls AWS directly, no server), §4.6/§4.8 and §5 (fleet_id on every resource; several fleets per account) */}
    <p>Your laptop and every agent sit inside your Tailscale tailnet, and that is the only way to reach an agent. Agents can reach the internet outbound; nothing on the internet can connect in. The app and CLI manage the fleet through AWS API calls straight to your account, with no hermetic server in between. Everything a fleet owns carries its fleet id, so several fleets can share one account.</p>
  </SectionHead>
  {/* Diagram labels: design.md §2 (laptop/AWS topology), §3.1 (one core behind app and CLI), §4.7 (STS check), §4.8 (fleet directory), §5 (foundation stack, agents/events tables, bucket, gateway endpoints, VPC public or nat mode), §5.1 (one IAM role per fleet; SSM /hermes/<fleet_id>/), §5.2 (tailnet policy entries), §6.2 (join key), §7.2 (0 inbound rules, nftables, direct WireGuard vs DERP), §7.3 (Chrome, noVNC), §9.1 (kept volume). */}
  <div class="dg-wrap">
<svg class="dg" viewBox="0 0 1280 860" role="img" aria-labelledby="dg-t dg-d">
<title id="dg-t">How hermetic fits together</title>
<desc id="dg-d">The desktop app and CLI on your laptop share one core that calls your AWS account directly. A CloudFormation foundation holds the fleet's tables, bucket and IAM role. Each agent runs on its own EC2 instance inside a security group with no inbound rules, with memory on a separate EBS volume. Your laptop and every agent sit inside the same Tailscale tailnet, which is the only way to reach an agent. Agents reach the internet outbound, and inbound traffic from the internet is dropped. AWS API calls, and the reads agents make from S3 and DynamoDB, go to AWS directly and stay outside the tailnet.</desc>
<defs>
