  <div class="dg-legend"><span><i></i>AWS API call, outside the tailnet</span><span><i class="pull"></i>box reads and reports</span><span><i class="fl"></i>fleet</span><span><i class="tn"></i>tailnet</span><span><i class="ts"></i>WireGuard link</span><span><i class="out"></i>outbound from the box</span><span><i class="blk"></i>inbound, dropped</span></div>
  <div class="dg-steps">
    {/* design.md §4.7 (STS, fleet id, foundation), §5.1 (OAuth secret at /hermetic/<fleet_id>/tailscale/oauth-secret in SSM) */}
    <div><b>1</b><h4>Init</h4><p>The app or CLI checks your AWS account with STS, gives the fleet an id, creates its foundation stack and stores your Tailscale OAuth client secret in SSM.</p></div>
    {/* design.md §6.2 Create (PutItem, SSM ts-key slot, config tarball to S3, CreateVolume, RunInstances) */}
    <div><b>2</b><h4>Create an agent</h4><p>Core records the agent in DynamoDB, uploads its config to S3, puts a Tailscale join key in SSM, then launches the instance and attaches a data volume.</p></div>
    {/* design.md §6.3 First boot, §2 (heartbeat to DynamoDB; S3 via gateway endpoint), §7.2 (S3 and DynamoDB through gateway endpoints) */}
    <div><b>3</b><h4>Boot</h4><p><code>hermeticd</code> pulls its config and its own secrets, installs Hermes, and writes heartbeats back to DynamoDB through the gateway endpoints.</p></div>
    {/* design.md §5.2 (tag:hermetic), §3.4 (noVNC and Hermes dashboard over Serve), §7.2 (Tailscale SSH), §9.2 Chat */}
    <div><b>4</b><h4>Operate</h4><p>The box joins your tailnet as <code>tag:hermetic</code>. Chat, logs, SSH, the Hermes dashboard and the remote desktop all travel over it.</p></div>
    {/* design.md §7.2 (no inbound SG rules; Tailscale connects outbound), §1 */}
    <div><b>5</b><h4>Stay sealed</h4><p>Nothing on the internet can open a connection to the box. Tailscale dials out from the box, so the security group never needs an inbound rule.</p></div>
  </div>
</section>
